  "newTunnel": "New tunnel",
  "newsConnectionBody": "If the server goes away, it shows within seconds and the connection comes back by itself; with a persistent session, you get back to the same terminal in tmux. While connecting and reconnecting, the way to the host, animated.",
  "newsConnectionTitle": "A connection that stays aware",
  "newsEditorBody": "Inherited values show with a dashed border and where they come from; type over one to change it, and ↺ inherits it again. Advanced settings stay folded. The same in groups, and the same grid in identities.",
  "newsEditorTitle": "A clearer host editor",
  "newsEnvBody": "Mark a group as Production, Testing or with a name and color of your own: its tabs and terminals say so, so as not to type into the wrong server.",
  "newsEnvTitle": "Each server's environment in sight",
  "newsFavoritesBody": "The star on hover over a host: at the top of the sidebar, in the rail, in the palette and on the start page, in the order you give them.",
  "newsFavoritesTitle": "Favorites",
  "newsFocusBody": "The sidebar folds to a rail of icons or hides ({keys}), by itself when a session opens if you like, and when hidden it shows as the pointer rests on the edge. Drag its edge to change its width; the terminal has more margin. All in Settings › General.",
  "newsFocusTitle": "More room for the terminal",
  "newsFresh": "new",
  "newsHopsBody": "Through a jump host, the latency card tells how long each hop takes, to see which part of the route is slow.",
  "newsHopsTitle": "Each hop's latency",
  "newsIdentitiesBody": "A user, keys and an agent with a name, for a whole group or several hosts at once.",
  "newsIdentitiesTitle": "Identities",
  "newsImportBody": "Hosts, groups, identities and tunnels from Termius, PuTTY, KiTTY, MobaXterm, Tabby or SecureCRT, and hosts from a CSV, from “…” › Import… in the sidebar. Passwords do not come along.",
  "newsImportTitle": "Import from your previous client",
  "newsKeysBody": "Make Ed25519, ECDSA or RSA keys, import yours, see their fingerprints and put them on a server without leaving OpenWard, as ssh-copy-id does.",
  "newsKeysTitle": "Keys",
  "newsLatencyBody": "The status bar shows how long the server takes to answer, with a chart of the last checks; amber when it rises well above the usual. Hover for the route and the cipher.",
  "newsLatencyTitle": "Latency in sight",
  "newsLinesBody": "A host can be SSH, Telnet or a serial port of this computer, for a switch's or a router's console. “Serial port” on the start page opens one by hand. Telnet warns that it is not encrypted.",
  "newsLinesTitle": "Telnet and serial ports",
  "newsLogoBody": "Umbral, an open O with a chevron: in the app's icon and, inside, on the welcome, the start page, About and here, in your theme's color.",
  "newsLogoTitle": "A new logo",
  "newsLogsBody": "Every connection leaves its entry in Session logs ({shortcut}): where, when and how it ended. Where you turn it on (Settings › Logs, or a group or a host), also what appeared on screen, to search it, watch it again command by command and export it. Never what you type; off by default while it is not encrypted.",
  "@newsLogsBody": {
    "placeholders": {
      "shortcut": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "newsLogsTitle": "Session logs",
  "newsManyHostsBody": "A snippet on the hosts you pick, each in its pane; a snippet on connecting, inherited; and in SFTP, “Open with…”: you edit it here and it goes up when you save it.",
  "newsManyHostsTitle": "Snippets on several hosts",
  "newsMoreThemesBody": "Monitor, with real green letters; Berenjena, with an aubergine terminal; Búnker, all in one phosphor; Marino, green on navy; and Catppuccin, Dracula and Tokyo Night for the whole window. In Settings › Appearance.",
  "newsMoreThemesTitle": "Seven more theme families",
  "newsMoshBody": "In a host's “Advanced”: the session goes on when you change networks or the laptop sleeps. It uses the mosh-client you have installed, and without UDP it goes on over SSH.",
  "newsMoshTitle": "Mosh, if you want it",
  "newsPaletteBody": "Everything the window does, your hosts, snippets and the commands you ran, a few letters away ({shortcut}). The history stays on this computer and never keeps passwords.",
  "@newsPaletteBody": {
    "placeholders": {
      "shortcut": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "newsPaletteTitle": "Command palette and history",
  "newsPanesBody": "Split a tab ({split}) or drag another one, or a host, onto a terminal; type into several panes at once ({broadcast}). With exit, the tab closes by itself.",
  "newsPanesBody2": "Dragging a tab onto a terminal no longer moves the window. Each pane's menu moves it to its own tab, swaps it or evens the sizes ({keys}); a new pane offers the open tabs, each pane has its name and the border between them shows and can be grabbed.",
  "newsPanesTitle": "Panes and broadcast",
  "newsPanesTitle2": "Panes without guessing",
  "newsSearchBody": "{keys} opens the palette with the open tabs, recent connections, hosts, actions and what you ran before. Start with > for actions only.",
  "newsSearchTitle": "One shortcut to find anything",
  "newsSecurityKeysBody": "Keys on a YubiKey or another FIDO2 key: made in “New key”, and on connecting the app asks for the touch and the PIN. Certificates about to run out say so in their last week.",
  "newsSecurityKeysTitle": "Security keys",
  "newsSftpBody": "Drag between this computer and the server, with a queue, resuming, and what already exists settled your way ({shortcut}).",
  "newsSftpTitle": "Two-pane SFTP",
  "newsShortcutsBody": "{keys} opens the list of shortcuts, with search, and buttons tell theirs on hover.",
  "newsShortcutsTitle": "Every shortcut at hand",
  "newsSidebarBody": "Every host is in Hosts ({keys}), with filters by environment, tag and system. The sidebar keeps what you use every day: what is open, the favorites and the recent ones, with the Library in one row; folded to a rail, what is open fits in a counter.",
  "newsSidebarTitle": "Hosts on their own page",
  "newsSnippetsBody": "Commands with variables one shortcut away ({shortcut}), and the keys you trust, with those of ~/.ssh/known_hosts.",
  "newsSnippetsTitle": "Snippets and known hosts",
  "newsStartBody": "Quick connect completes with your hosts and the addresses you have used; below, recent connections with how long they lasted, and the open tunnels.",
  "newsStartTitle": "A start page to get back to work",
  "newsSuggestBody": "What comes next shows in gray, from that host's history, your snippets and common commands; → types it. All on this computer.",
  "newsSuggestTitle": "Suggestions as you type",
  "newsSystemBody2": "Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora, Alpine and 22 more systems, by their logo in the color of their environment; macOS and Windows, by an icon of their own. For the ones that do not say it when connecting, such as those behind Tailscale SSH, “Find out the system” in their menu reads /etc/os-release; or on every host, from Settings › General.",
  "newsSystemTitle2": "Each server's system, by its logo",
  "newsTerminalBody": "Copy on select, paste with a right click, errors and addresses in color, a Mac's or a PC's shortcuts. Per host: the character set (Latin-1, CP437…), Backspace and colors of its own.",
  "newsTerminalTitle": "The terminal your way",
  "newsThemesBody": "Five themes in light and dark, layers that mix, text size, minimum contrast and reduced motion.",
  "newsThemesTitle": "Themes and visual accessibility",
  "newsTunnelsBody": "Local, remote and SOCKS5, opened on connect; and HTTP and SOCKS5 proxies to reach the server.",
  "newsTunnelsTitle": "Saved tunnels and proxy",
  "newsWorkspacesBody": "Save your tabs and panes by name and open them again, connected, from the library or the palette.",
  "newsWorkspacesTitle": "Workspaces",
